Verified source invariants and exact touchpoints
- artifact_dagger_process.rs:100–219: validates explicit roots, request and fixed environment; verifies executable bytes/full canonical module manifest; copies retained private snapshots/request; fixed argv only; env_clear plus private HOME/XDG/temp. Task text is not command/argv interpolation.
- artifact_dagger_process.rs:135–198,449–519: exclusion lock, consumed record and global pending fence durably precede spawn. Attempt-only consumed identity cannot be bypassed by changed request/binding. Pending or incomplete/corrupt history fences other identities and restart; no reconciliation or pruning path.
- artifact_dagger_process.rs:224–271,724–866: concurrent bounded nonblocking captures, finite TERM/KILL cleanup reserve and owned-group handling. Positive independent verifier, local reap/group absence and remaining original deadline are all necessary to clear pending. UnknownQuiescence stays Unknown; exit0/module JSON never establishes engine cleanup. Injected verifier must honor its documented deadline/cancellation contract; ordinary filesystem syscalls are not hard-real-time cancellable.
- artifact_dagger.rs:274–358: cleanup/identity/size validation precedes accepting transport output. Exit0 can carry typed failed envelopes; nonzero exit is protocol failure, not authentication inference. New policy_denied/prerequisite outcomes terminate without repair/fallback. Produced text alone never advances pipeline acceptance.
- main.py:119–142: exported wrapper bounds request File before contents and hashes original bytes; obtains trusted assets via SDK module source, not package __file__. Missing/corrupt assets/query failures fail closed without raw diagnostics. Actual scalar/File CLI interoperability is not claimed.
- main.py:62–113 and graph.py:86–117: exported Setup evaluates fixed no-model version/probe/baseline checker nodes. Readiness requires exact observed version, exits, UID/GID/Python/workspace and byte hashes plus complete expected checker failures, not constants or a passing baseline fiction.
- main.py:26–48,132–139: Execute cannot construct inference graph and returns policy_denied for valid requests. Submit recomputes bindings/checks but returns prerequisite even for a passing deterministic candidate; supplied review claims cannot fabricate semantic review.
- artifacts.py:10–116: exact bounded candidate/base/patch/response/checker hashing and reconstruction; trusted checker is recomputed. main.py:14–23 compiles the same trusted checker byte snapshot whose hash is retained; candidate text is interpreted only by restricted checker.
- graph.py:39–50,127–165: default model/provider, clean fixed environment, no credentials/model override/session reuse; coding/checker/review sibling separation and attempt/request identity inputs. Inference graph has no exported caller and no request-level egress enable switch.
- dagger.json/pyproject.toml/image/Dockerfile: fixed engine/SDK/OpenCode source recipe; image context is image/ only. Ubuntu tag/apt and SDK asset acquisition are not hermetic/live-verified; documentation explicitly preserves these limits.

